<title>INDIA: Indian gold steady, imports from Middle East slow.</title>
<headline>Indian gold steady, imports from Middle East slow.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>** Gold 24 carat closed 15 rupees higher at 4,845 per 10 grammes as wedding season demand met slower imports from Middle East due to Islamic festival.</p>
<p>** Gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) closed 200 rupees higher at 56,700. They were up by 400 rupees per piece on Tuesday while market was closed on Wednesday for Hindu festival.</p>
<p>** Silver (.999) closed 20 rupees higher at 7,000 rupees per kg on the back of speculative buying prompted by uptrend in the world market. Physical demand was dull.</p>
<p>--  </p>
